WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.870
Every day, the tide floods in, and a
whole forest stands in salty water.

2
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.930
When it drains away, the
roots stand in low-oxygen mud,

3
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.250
where slow water lets
fine sediment settle.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:19.130
These are mangroves: 14.8
million hectares of them in 2020,

5
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.010
nearly 44 per cent in
South and Southeast Asia.

6
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.970
Mangroves cannot withstand
freezing temperatures.

7
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.770
So how can anything live there?

8
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.630
Are the trees dead?

9
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.590
Do only worms survive?

10
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.050
In this mission, you'll map
four coastal ecosystems,

11
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.590
from coral reefs to sand dunes.

12
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.570
Then you'll separate a mangrove forest's
living parts from its non-living ones.

13
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:48.200
Your mission: find out how life survives
in a forest the tide floods every day.
